{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Add the self-contained rebar MCP HTTP service to the box per the ADR (deft-evolutive-mosasaur):\na new `mcp` compose service + `Dockerfile.mcp` running loopback-published `rebar-mcp` HTTP, and an\nnginx `/mcp/` TLS-edge location with a **switchable upstream** so the autodeploy slice\n(panicky-sylphish-foxterrier) can flip traffic blue→green atomically. INFRA only; the live AWS\nprovision/deploy is approval-gated (a human performs it). Single concern: the on-box MCP service\nand its edge — autodeploy logic lives in foxterrier, secrets in avians.\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`: an `mcp` service (image built from `Dockerfile.mcp`),\n  loopback-published on a new dedicated host port (127.0.0.1:8091; Gerrit owns 8080, review-bot\n  REVIEW_BOT_PORT, opcert 8090), `restart: always`, with a container `healthcheck` hitting the MCP\n  `/health` endpoint, and a `stop_grace_period` sized to cover the app's SIGTERM grace window. The\n  ADR-decided fail-closed HTTP posture is set via env: `REBAR_MCP_TRANSPORT=http`,\n  `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_TLS_AT_EDGE=true`, `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS`/`REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`\n  (the external host / origin), `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ENABLED=1`, `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STRATEGIES=static`,\n  `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL`, `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STATIC_TOKENS_FILE`. `MCP_PATHS` for the\n  autodeploy change-detector is declared here (as a compose comment) so foxterrier can consume it.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp`: builds `rebar-mcp` from the same repo-root build context +\n  committed `uv.lock` as `Dockerfile.opcert` (`python:3.12-slim`,\n  `uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra mcp`). CMD boots the http transport\n  (`rebar-mcp` with `REBAR_MCP_TRANSPORT=http`). A container `HEALTHCHECK` curls the loopback\n  `/health`. Boots with `transport=http`, `http_tls_at_edge=true`, allowed hosts/origins,\n  `auth_resource_server_url`, `static` verifier — the ADR-0050 fail-closed guards\n  (DNS-rebinding/Origin, non-loopback-bind ack).\n- `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`: a new `location /mcp/` proxying to a named `upstream rebar_mcp`\n  block whose single `server` line is a **materialized include** (the atomic-flip seam). TLS\n  terminates at nginx (mirrors `/review/` + the header-guarded `/opcert/`).\n- `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (NEW, committed seed): the initial (blue) upstream target\n  `server 127.0.0.1:8091;`. See the fresh-boot materialization contract below.\n- A `/health` endpoint on the MCP server exposing an integer `in_flight` gauge that counts ONLY\n  long-running/certified ops (review_plan/verify_completion/review_code/scan_spec), plus a bounded\n  SIGTERM grace window so a retiring container lets an in-flight op finish before exit. The gauge\n  feeds foxterrier's retire check; it does not gate the deploy. New health/gauge/signal code lives\n  in a NEW module `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` (mcp_server.py is at its 800-LOC cap), wired from\n  `build_server`/`main`.\n\n## nginx switchable-upstream materialization (fresh boot + atomic flip)\nThe `/mcp/` upstream is atomically re-pointable by foxterrier. Unlike the `/opcert/` guard `map`\n(whose `default 0` makes a zero-match GLOB include safe), an nginx `upstream {}` with **zero**\n`server` lines is a **config error** (`nginx -t` fails: \"no servers are inside upstream\"). So the\ntemplate uses a GLOB include `include /etc/nginx/mcp-upstream*.conf;` (zero-match-tolerant, mirroring\nthe `opcert-guard*.conf` glob) AND this change ships a **committed seed** `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf`\nthat the **host-side deploy/boot render step** installs. That render step — the SAME `envsubst`\nconsumer documented in the template header that produces `/etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf` and that\n`infra/scripts/compose-up.sh` uses to materialize `/etc/nginx/opcert-guard.map.conf` — ALSO copies\n`infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` to `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` BEFORE the first `nginx -t` / load.\nThus on a fresh boot (before foxterrier's first flip) the upstream has exactly one backend\n(127.0.0.1:8091) and `nginx -t` passes; a MISSING include file would leave the upstream empty and\nFAIL `nginx -t`, which is precisely why the seed is committed and installed at boot rather than left\nto first-deploy. foxterrier's blue→green cutover re-points by atomically rewriting that single\n`/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (the `current`-pointer analog) + `nginx -s reload`. The AC's\n`nginx -t` verification renders the template WITH the seed include present.\n\n## Approach + rationale\nMirror the proven opcert edge (loopback service + nginx location) but expose a switchable upstream\nrather than a hardcoded `proxy_pass host:port`, because the ADR's blue-green cutover needs to\nre-point the upstream atomically (the local updater's `current`-pointer analog). `/health` counts\nonly expensive ops so retirement waits on billable work, not trivial reads. Shared base image keeps\ndisk/build cost low; the extra retained MCP images are bounded by the existing docker prune.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tier: **in-process ASGI integration** (docker NOT required): `/health` served by the FastMCP\n  `streamable_http_app` returns a JSON body with an integer `in_flight` field. Oracle: `in_flight`\n  reads 0 at idle, increments while a simulated long-running certified op runs (a stubbed certified\n  tool held in flight), and returns to 0 after — asserted via the real endpoint through a Starlette\n  TestClient; a trivial read op does NOT move the gauge (contrast case). If docker is available the\n  container `healthcheck` against `/health` may additionally be exercised, but the AC does not\n  depend on it.\n- [ ] Fail-closed boot: with a non-loopback bind and NO TLS-at-edge/allowlist ack, `build_server`\n  refuses to start (raises `McpStartupError` with the ADR-0050 guard message); with the ack +\n  `static` verifier it boots. Oracle: the existing `_resolve_http_runtime` gates, asserted directly.\n- [ ] The nginx `/mcp/` location proxies to a named `upstream rebar_mcp` block whose `server` line\n  is sourced from a materialized include (`mcp-upstream*.conf`), and a committed seed\n  `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` supplies the initial target so `nginx -t` passes on the rendered\n  template. Oracle: structural parse of the rendered template (nginx binary not required in CI);\n  `nginx -t` when a binary is available.\n- [ ] SIGTERM grace: sending SIGTERM while the `in_flight` gauge is > 0 lets the op finish within\n  the bounded grace window before the process exits (subprocess/signal test), not an immediate kill.\n\n## Testing\nIn-process ASGI tests (Starlette TestClient over `streamable_http_app`) for `/health` idle/inflight/\ncontrast; direct `build_server` assertions for the fail-closed gates; a structural parse of the\nrendered nginx template for the named-upstream-from-materialized-include seam; a subprocess/signal\ntest for the SIGTERM grace window. No docker dependency.\n\n## File impact\n`infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` (new), `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`,\n`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`, `infra/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` (new),\n`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` (new), `src/rebar/mcp_server.py`, and tests under `tests/`.\n\n## Compat / rollback\nPurely additive — new service, new port, new nginx location; touches no existing service. Rollback =\nremove the `mcp` service/location + seed include (gerrit/review-bot/opcert unaffected). Security\ntrust-boundary: new authenticated network endpoint — enforced by `static` bearer at the app + TLS at\nthe nginx edge.\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR). Blocks: panicky-sylphish-foxterrier (needs the\nswitchable upstream + `/health`), unmythical-uninspired-olm (needs a reachable endpoint)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787611558572862001,"uuid":"b6515011-9e81-45b3-a01d-0707fc8b3349"}